# Start the streaming software

- Double click the <span style="color:lightcoral; font-weight:bold">vMix (x64)</span> icon on the left side of the screen.
- At the top of the screen, click the <span style="color:lightcoral; font-weight:bold">DownArrow</span> to the right of the <span style="color:lightcoral; font-weight:bold">OpenButton</span> and select the <span style="color:#FF0000; font-weight:bold">Preset Setup IV.vmix</span>.
- At the top of the screen, click the <span style="color:lightcoral; font-weight:bold">MaximizeIcon</span>, the second icon from the right. This should make everything smaller. Click and drag the window to the left edge of the screen. Resize so that the window touches the top, left, and bottom edges of the screen.

![select Preset Setup IV.vmix](../fot/preset_setup.png)

- You should see this:

![screen_after_preset_setup](../fot/preset_setup_result.png)

- Click on the <span style="color:lightcoral; font-weight:bold">GearIcon</span>for preset 11.

<img src="../fot/gear_icon_eleven.png" alt="gear icon for preset 11" width="400">

- In the input/output window, left column, press on <span style="color:lightcoral; font-weight:bold">PTZ</span>.

<img src="../fot/ptz.png" alt="select PTZ" width="400">

- Resize this window as appropriate. Move this window to the right so that it does not overlap with the main window and the controls are accessbile.
- The screen should look as follows.

![screen layout ready](../fot/screen_layout_ready.png)

- The left preview window should have an amber bar. The preset 6 window should have an amber bar. The right preview window should have a green bar. The preset 11 window should have a green bar.

