# Begin audio and video streaming

- Click on the Stream button; the button bar turns red
- Click on the Record button; it will have a red STREAM2 & REC button by top preview
- The FADE button is used to transition between camera 1 and camera 2
- The active camera is on the right with a green bar
- The other camera preview is on the left with an amber bar
- If the streaming stops for any reason, do not restart it because of how YouTube is set up. Change the file name in the record button (if it has stopped) and restart recording only, not streaming.

# Cameras

- Camera 1 is at the left side of the main aisle, near the front, and points to the right lectern, the organist, and the choir.
- Camera 2 is at the back of the church and points up the center aisle.

# Microphones

- Fr. Bill uses "wireless 5" microphone (slider 13/14 on the sound board). He often forgets to turn it off. Be prepared to turn down the input setting.
- Fr. Ryan uses "wireless 6" microphone (slider 15/16 on the sound board). He is very good about how he uses his microphone.

# Correct left preview screen setting

The correct way to set the left preview screen is:

1. Click on the left screen
2. Click on the desired gear to control the camera
3. Click on the desired preset

# Camera control for right preview screen

If the right preview screen does not have the correct camera controls:

1. Click on the right screen
2. Click the desired gear to control the camera

